-- (8)(g): a guarantee or security by a subsidiary of a borrowing corporation. Arguments: the corporation is or will be liable to repay money; the money came from an invitation to the public for debentures; board control; voting power; subsidiary of a subsidiary; the act is a guarantee; the act is security; good faith; ordinary course of commercial dealing.
