-- Cases for the seat layer sgh-seat.l4: every case calls one seat question with plain inputs and states the answer the text gives.
-- Each case is a layer-1 test of the same function, carried over with its expected value (written from the text beside the assertion in the layer-1 tests file).
-- A yes case, the text's no case where there is one, and a not-covered case where there is one are all present wherever the layer-1 tests have them.

§ `Part 2: the Registrar's acts (section 8)`

-- Under section 8(2), is an act of a Deputy or Assistant Registrar as valid and effectual as if the Registrar had done or signed it
#ASSERT `Under section 8(2), is an act of a Deputy or Assistant Registrar as valid and effectual as if the Registrar had done or signed it` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- all three: "may be done or signed by any such Deputy or Assistant Registrar and is as valid and effectual as if done or signed by the Registrar"
#ASSERT `Under section 8(2), is an act of a Deputy or Assistant Registrar as valid and effectual as if the Registrar had done or signed it` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not an act the Act gives the Registrar: the text does not say
#ASSERT `Under section 8(2), is an act of a Deputy or Assistant Registrar as valid and effectual as if the Registrar had done or signed it` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- done by someone other than a Deputy or Assistant Registrar: the text does not say
#ASSERT `Under section 8(2), is an act of a Deputy or Assistant Registrar as valid and effectual as if the Registrar had done or signed it` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- outside the direction and control or the prescribed restrictions: "Subject to ..." limits the grant, the text does not say the act is invalid
#ASSERT `Under section 8(2), is an act of a Deputy or Assistant Registrar as valid and effectual as if the Registrar had done or signed it` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- none

-- Under section 8(3), do I need to be concerned to see or inquire about prescribed restrictions or limitations on a Deputy or Assistant Registrar when I deal with one
#ASSERT `Under section 8(3), do I need to be concerned to see or inquire about prescribed restrictions or limitations on a Deputy or Assistant Registrar when I deal with one` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "No person dealing with any Deputy or Assistant Registrar needs to be concerned to see or inquire"
#ASSERT `Under section 8(3), do I need to be concerned to see or inquire about prescribed restrictions or limitations on a Deputy or Assistant Registrar when I deal with one` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a person not dealing with a Deputy or Assistant Registrar: the text does not say

-- Under section 8(3), is an act or omission of a Deputy or Assistant Registrar as valid and effectual, so far as it affects me, as if the Registrar had done or omitted it
#ASSERT `Under section 8(3), is an act or omission of a Deputy or Assistant Registrar as valid and effectual, so far as it affects me, as if the Registrar had done or omitted it` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "every act or omission of a Deputy or Assistant Registrar so far as it affects any such person is as valid and effectual"
#ASSERT `Under section 8(3), is an act or omission of a Deputy or Assistant Registrar as valid and effectual, so far as it affects me, as if the Registrar had done or omitted it` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an act that does not affect the person
#ASSERT `Under section 8(3), is an act or omission of a Deputy or Assistant Registrar as valid and effectual, so far as it affects me, as if the Registrar had done or omitted it` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an act of someone who is not a Deputy or Assistant Registrar
#ASSERT `Under section 8(3), is an act or omission of a Deputy or Assistant Registrar as valid and effectual, so far as it affects me, as if the Registrar had done or omitted it` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- neither

-- Under section 8(4), is a court or tribunal to take judicial notice of the seal or signature on a document I rely on
#ASSERT `Under section 8(4), is a court or tribunal to take judicial notice of the seal or signature on a document I rely on` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "All courts, judges and persons acting judicially are to take judicial notice of the seal and signature of the Registrar and of any Deputy or Assistant Registrar"
#ASSERT `Under section 8(4), is a court or tribunal to take judicial notice of the seal or signature on a document I rely on` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a court, judge or person acting judicially: the text does not say
#ASSERT `Under section 8(4), is a court or tribunal to take judicial notice of the seal or signature on a document I rely on` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- some other seal or signature: the text does not say
#ASSERT `Under section 8(4), is a court or tribunal to take judicial notice of the seal or signature on a document I rely on` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- neither

§ `Part 2: inspection of books, warrants, copies as evidence, destroying documents (sections 8A to 8D)`

-- Under section 8A(1), does the Minister have power to require the corporation to produce its books
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(1), does the Minister have power to require the corporation to produce its books` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "Where the Minister is satisfied that there is good reason for so doing, the Minister may ... give directions ... to produce such books relating to the affairs of a corporation"
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(1), does the Minister have power to require the corporation to produce its books` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the Minister is not satisfied: a failed "where" (periods ruling (b); split site (ii))
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(1), does the Minister have power to require the corporation to produce its books` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not satisfied and other books: the gate fails first
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(1), does the Minister have power to require the corporation to produce its books` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- satisfied but the books do not relate to the affairs of a corporation: the power is over "such books relating to the affairs of a corporation"

-- Under section 8A(2), do the Minister or an authorised person have the like power to require me to produce the books
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(2), do the Minister or an authorised person have the like power to require me to produce the books` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "the Minister or that authorised person has the like power to require production of those books from any person who appears ... to be in possession of them"
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(2), do the Minister or an authorised person have the like power to require me to produce the books` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no power under (1): a failed "where"
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(2), do the Minister or an authorised person have the like power to require me to produce the books` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the person does not appear to be in possession: the text does not say

-- Under section 8A(2), is the production of the books without prejudice to my lien on them
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(2), is the production of the books without prejudice to my lien on them` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "where any such person claims a lien on any books produced by the person, the production is without prejudice to the lien"
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(2), is the production of the books without prejudice to my lien on them` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no lien claimed: the text does not say

-- Under section 8A(3)(a)(i), does the power to require production include making copies of, or taking extracts from, the books
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(3)(a)(i), does the power to require production include making copies of, or taking extracts from, the books` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(a) if the books are produced -- (i) to make copies of, or take extracts from, them"
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(3)(a)(i), does the power to require production include making copies of, or taking extracts from, the books` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the books are not produced: the power "includes" and the list is open

-- Under section 8A(3)(a)(ii), does the power include requiring me to provide an explanation of the books
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(3)(a)(ii), does the power include requiring me to provide an explanation of the books` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(ii) to require that person who is a present or past officer of, or who is or was at any time employed by the corporation to provide an explanation of any of them"
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(3)(a)(ii), does the power include requiring me to provide an explanation of the books` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a person who is neither: the text does not say
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(3)(a)(ii), does the power include requiring me to provide an explanation of the books` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the books are not produced

-- Under section 8A(3)(b), does the power include requiring me to state where the books are
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(3)(b), does the power include requiring me to state where the books are` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(b) if the books are not produced, to require the person required to produce them to state, to the best of the person's knowledge and belief, where they are"
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(3)(b), does the power include requiring me to state where the books are` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the books are produced: the power "includes" and the list is open

-- Under section 8A(4), may my statement be used in evidence against me
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(4), may my statement be used in evidence against me` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "A statement made by a person in compliance with a requirement imposed by this section may be used in evidence against the person"
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(4), may my statement be used in evidence against me` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a statement made otherwise: the subsection does not speak

-- Under section 8A(5), does the power to make the requirement extend to me as an officer of the body corporate
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(5), does the power to make the requirement extend to me as an officer of the body corporate` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a body corporate in the course of being wound up (or dissolved) and an individual who is or has been its officer
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(5), does the power to make the requirement extend to me as an officer of the body corporate` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not an officer of the body corporate
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(5), does the power to make the requirement extend to me as an officer of the body corporate` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the person is not (or was not) a body corporate

-- Under section 8A(6), am I guilty of the offence of not complying with a requirement imposed by virtue of section 8A
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(6), am I guilty of the offence of not complying with a requirement imposed by virtue of section 8A` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "If a requirement ... imposed by virtue of this section is not complied with, the corporation or other person on whom the requirement was imposed shall be guilty of an offence"
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(6), am I guilty of the offence of not complying with a requirement imposed by virtue of section 8A` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- complied with: an element is unmet (split site (i))
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(6), am I guilty of the offence of not complying with a requirement imposed by virtue of section 8A` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no requirement was imposed: an element is unmet

-- Under section 8A(6), what is the most I may be sentenced to on conviction
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(6), what is the most I may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF 2000, 6, TRUE, FALSE)   -- "a fine not exceeding $2,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both"
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(6), what is the most I may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not guilty: no penalty stated
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(6), what is the most I may be sentenced to on conviction` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no requirement imposed: no penalty stated

-- Under section 8A(7), does the subsection give me a defence on these facts
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(7), does the subsection give me a defence on these facts` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "it is a defence to prove that they were not in the person's possession or under the person's control"
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(7), does the subsection give me a defence on these facts` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "or that it was not reasonably practicable for the person to comply with the requirement"
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(7), does the subsection give me a defence on these facts` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- both proved
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(7), does the subsection give me a defence on these facts` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- neither proved: this section gives no defence on these facts (delegated-defences ruling (b))
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(7), does the subsection give me a defence on these facts` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not charged under (6): a failed "Where a person is charged"
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(7), does the subsection give me a defence on these facts` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the requirement was to give an explanation or a statement, not to produce books: the gate "in respect of a requirement to produce any books" fails

-- Under section 8A(8), am I guilty of the offence of giving a false or misleading explanation or statement in purported compliance
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(8), am I guilty of the offence of giving a false or misleading explanation or statement in purported compliance` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "which the person knows to be false or misleading in a material particular"
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(8), am I guilty of the offence of giving a false or misleading explanation or statement in purported compliance` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "or recklessly provides or makes an explanation or a statement which is false or misleading in a material particular"
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(8), am I guilty of the offence of giving a false or misleading explanation or statement in purported compliance` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- false but neither knew nor reckless: an element is unmet (split site (i))
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(8), am I guilty of the offence of giving a false or misleading explanation or statement in purported compliance` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not false or misleading in a material particular
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(8), am I guilty of the offence of giving a false or misleading explanation or statement in purported compliance` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not provided in purported compliance with a requirement imposed by section 8A

-- Under section 8A(8), what is the most I may be sentenced to on conviction
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(8), what is the most I may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF 20000, 24, TRUE, FALSE)   -- "a fine not exceeding $20,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to both" (24 months)
#ASSERT `Under section 8A(8), what is the most I may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not guilty: no penalty stated

-- Under section 8B(1), may a Magistrate issue a warrant authorising a police officer to enter my premises, search them and take possession of the books
#ASSERT `Under section 8B(1), may a Magistrate issue a warrant authorising a police officer to enter my premises, search them and take possession of the books` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "If a Magistrate is satisfied, on information on oath or affirmation laid by an authorised person, that there are reasonable grounds for suspecting ... the Magistrate may issue a warrant"
#ASSERT `Under section 8B(1), may a Magistrate issue a warrant authorising a police officer to enter my premises, search them and take possession of the books` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- information not laid by an authorised person: a failed "if" gating a grant (grant ruling, limit 1)
#ASSERT `Under section 8B(1), may a Magistrate issue a warrant authorising a police officer to enter my premises, search them and take possession of the books` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the Magistrate is not satisfied: a failed "if" gating a grant
#ASSERT `Under section 8B(1), may a Magistrate issue a warrant authorising a police officer to enter my premises, search them and take possession of the books` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the books have been produced: a failed "if" gating a grant

-- Under section 8B(2), is the warrant in force on the date I ask about
#ASSERT `Under section 8B(2), is the warrant in force on the date I ask about` (Date 10 3 2025) (Date 10 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- issued 10 March 2025, asked on the day it was issued: in force ("continues in force until the end of the period of one month after the date on which it was issued")
#ASSERT `Under section 8B(2), is the warrant in force on the date I ask about` (Date 10 3 2025) (Date 10 4 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the last day of one month after 10 March is 10 April: in force on 10 April
#ASSERT `Under section 8B(2), is the warrant in force on the date I ask about` (Date 10 3 2025) (Date 11 4 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- one day later: the period fixed in the text's own words has ended (periods ruling (a))
#ASSERT `Under section 8B(2), is the warrant in force on the date I ask about` (Date 10 3 2025) (Date 9 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the day before it was issued: outside the period
#ASSERT `Under section 8B(2), is the warrant in force on the date I ask about` (Date 31 1 2025) (Date 28 2 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- issued 31 January: one month after is 28 February (P4: the month's last day), in force on 28 February
#ASSERT `Under section 8B(2), is the warrant in force on the date I ask about` (Date 31 1 2025) (Date 1 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- 1 March is after the last day, 28 February

-- Under section 8B(3), does taking possession of the books, or securing them against interference, prejudice my lien on them
#ASSERT `Under section 8B(3), does taking possession of the books, or securing them against interference, prejudice my lien on them` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "the taking of possession of the books or the securing of the books against interference does not prejudice the lien"
#ASSERT `Under section 8B(3), does taking possession of the books, or securing them against interference, prejudice my lien on them` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no one has a lien: the subsection does not speak
#ASSERT `Under section 8B(3), does taking possession of the books, or securing them against interference, prejudice my lien on them` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- books not taken or secured under section 8B

-- Under section 8B(4), does the person who took possession of the books have the power I ask about
#ASSERT `Under section 8B(4), does the person who took possession of the books have the power I ask about` `s 8B(4)(a) make copies of, or take extracts from, the books` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(a) may make copies of, or take extracts from, the books"
#ASSERT `Under section 8B(4), does the person who took possession of the books have the power I ask about` `s 8B(4)(b) require a person who was party to the compilation of the books to make a statement providing an explanation` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(b) may require any person who was party to the compilation of the books to make a statement"
#ASSERT `Under section 8B(4), does the person who took possession of the books have the power I ask about` `s 8B(4)(c) retain possession of the books for such period as is necessary for their inspection and for copies or extracts to be made by or on behalf of the Minister` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(c) may retain possession of the books for such period as is necessary"
#ASSERT `Under section 8B(4), does the person who took possession of the books have the power I ask about` `s 8B(4)(a) make copies of, or take extracts from, the books` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the person neither took possession nor holds delivered books: a failed "Where" (periods ruling (b); split site (ii))

-- Under section 8B(4)(d), must the person in possession of the books permit me, if I am entitled to inspect them, to inspect them at all reasonable times
#ASSERT `Under section 8B(4)(d), must the person in possession of the books permit me, if I am entitled to inspect them, to inspect them at all reasonable times` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "during that period must permit a person who would be entitled to inspect any one or more of those books ... to inspect at all reasonable times"
#ASSERT `Under section 8B(4)(d), must the person in possession of the books permit me, if I am entitled to inspect them, to inspect them at all reasonable times` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the person is not one who would be entitled to inspect: the duty's own question
#ASSERT `Under section 8B(4)(d), must the person in possession of the books permit me, if I am entitled to inspect them, to inspect them at all reasonable times` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- outside the period of retention: the duty's own question

-- Under section 8B(5), am I guilty of the offence of obstructing a right of entry, search or taking possession conferred by a warrant
#ASSERT `Under section 8B(5), am I guilty of the offence of obstructing a right of entry, search or taking possession conferred by a warrant` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "who obstructs the exercise of a right of entry or search conferred by virtue of a warrant issued under this section"
