-- Under section 12(6), may the Registrar destroy the document or transfer it to the National Archives of Singapore
#ASSERT `Under section 12(6), may the Registrar destroy the document or transfer it to the National Archives of Singapore` `s 12(6)(a) destroy the document with the authorisation of the National Library Board under section 17 of the National Library Board Act 1995` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(a) destroy the document with the authorisation of the National Library Board"
#ASSERT `Under section 12(6), may the Registrar destroy the document or transfer it to the National Archives of Singapore` `s 12(6)(a) destroy the document with the authorisation of the National Library Board under section 17 of the National Library Board Act 1995` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- destruction without the Board's authorisation
#ASSERT `Under section 12(6), may the Registrar destroy the document or transfer it to the National Archives of Singapore` `s 12(6)(b) transfer the document to the National Archives of Singapore under section 16 of that Act` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(b) transfer the document to the National Archives of Singapore": no Board authorisation is needed for a transfer
#ASSERT `Under section 12(6), may the Registrar destroy the document or transfer it to the National Archives of Singapore` `s 12(6)(b) transfer the document to the National Archives of Singapore under section 16 of that Act` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the Registrar is not of the opinion that it is no longer necessary or desirable to retain the document
#ASSERT `Under section 12(6), may the Registrar destroy the document or transfer it to the National Archives of Singapore` `s 12(6)(b) transfer the document to the National Archives of Singapore under section 16 of that Act` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not microfilmed or converted to electronic form

-- Under section 12(7), is the medium a non-electronic medium
#ASSERT `Under section 12(7), is the medium a non-electronic medium` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "'non-electronic medium' means a medium other than the electronic transaction system established under Part 6A"
#ASSERT `Under section 12(7), is the medium a non-electronic medium` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- any other medium

-- Under section 12A(1), is the system the electronic transaction system mentioned in section 12A(1)
#ASSERT `Under section 12A(1), is the system the electronic transaction system mentioned in section 12A(1)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "the electronic transaction system established under Part 6A of the Accounting and Corporate Regulatory Authority Act 2004"
#ASSERT `Under section 12A(1), is the system the electronic transaction system mentioned in section 12A(1)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another system: the text does not say

-- Under section 12A(1)(a), may the Registrar require or permit me to carry out the transaction using the electronic transaction system
#ASSERT `Under section 12A(1)(a), may the Registrar require or permit me to carry out the transaction using the electronic transaction system` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(a) require or permit any person to carry out any transaction with the Registrar under this Act"
#ASSERT `Under section 12A(1)(a), may the Registrar require or permit me to carry out the transaction using the electronic transaction system` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a transaction in the sense of subsection (4)

-- Under section 12A(1)(b), may the Registrar issue the document using the electronic transaction system
#ASSERT `Under section 12A(1)(b), may the Registrar issue the document using the electronic transaction system` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(b) issue any approval, certificate, notice, determination or other document pursuant or connected to a transaction"
#ASSERT `Under section 12A(1)(b), may the Registrar issue the document using the electronic transaction system` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- some other document

-- Under section 12A(2), may the Registrar cause the electronic transaction system and the registers to reflect the earlier date and time
#ASSERT `Under section 12A(2), may the Registrar cause the electronic transaction system and the registers to reflect the earlier date and time` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "If the Registrar is satisfied that a transaction should be treated as having been carried out at some date and time earlier"
#ASSERT `Under section 12A(2), may the Registrar cause the electronic transaction system and the registers to reflect the earlier date and time` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not satisfied: a failed "If" gating a grant (grant ruling, limit 1)

-- Under section 12A(3), must the Registrar keep a record of the alteration
#ASSERT `Under section 12A(3), must the Registrar keep a record of the alteration` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "The Registrar must keep a record whenever the electronic transaction system or the registers are altered under subsection (2)"
#ASSERT `Under section 12A(3), must the Registrar keep a record of the alteration` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not altered under (2): a failed "whenever" (counts as "where")

-- Under section 12A(4), is the thing a document
#ASSERT `Under section 12A(4), is the thing a document` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "'document' includes any application, form, report, certification, notice, confirmation, declaration, return or other document ... filed or lodged with, or submitted to, the Registrar"
#ASSERT `Under section 12A(4), is the thing a document` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "includes": the list is open

-- Under section 12A(4), is the act a transaction in relation to the Registrar
#ASSERT `Under section 12A(4), is the act a transaction in relation to the Registrar` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(a) the filing or lodging of any document with the Registrar"
#ASSERT `Under section 12A(4), is the act a transaction in relation to the Registrar` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(b) any making of any application, submission or request to the Registrar"
#ASSERT `Under section 12A(4), is the act a transaction in relation to the Registrar` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(c) any provision of any undertaking or declaration to the Registrar"
#ASSERT `Under section 12A(4), is the act a transaction in relation to the Registrar` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(d) any extraction, retrieval or accessing of any document, record or information maintained by the Registrar"
#ASSERT `Under section 12A(4), is the act a transaction in relation to the Registrar` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "'transaction', in relation to the Registrar, means" (a "means" definition)

§ `Rectifying the registers (sections 12B to 12D)`

-- Under section 12B(1), may the Court by order direct the Registrar to rectify the register
#ASSERT `Under section 12B(1), may the Court by order direct the Registrar to rectify the register` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "Where it appears to the Court, as a result of evidence adduced before it by an applicant company, that any particular recorded in a register is erroneous or defective, the Court may, by order, direct the Registrar to rectify the register"
#ASSERT `Under section 12B(1), may the Court by order direct the Registrar to rectify the register` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no evidence adduced by an applicant company: a failed "Where" (periods ruling (b); split site (ii))
#ASSERT `Under section 12B(1), may the Court by order direct the Registrar to rectify the register` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- it does not appear to the Court that the particular is erroneous or defective: a failed "Where"

-- Under section 12B(1), must the Registrar rectify the register accordingly on receipt of the order
#ASSERT `Under section 12B(1), must the Registrar rectify the register accordingly on receipt of the order` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "the Registrar must, upon receipt of the order, rectify the register accordingly"
#ASSERT `Under section 12B(1), must the Registrar rectify the register accordingly on receipt of the order` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no order received: a failed "upon" (counts as "where")

-- Under section 12B(2), must the applicant company file the fresh document with the Registrar together with a copy of the Court order and a copy of the Court application
#ASSERT `Under section 12B(2), must the applicant company file the fresh document with the Registrar together with a copy of the Court order and a copy of the Court application` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "An order ... may require that a fresh document, showing the rectification, must be filed by the applicant company with the Registrar together with a copy of the Court order, and a copy of the Court application": the order so requires
#ASSERT `Under section 12B(2), must the applicant company file the fresh document with the Registrar together with a copy of the Court order and a copy of the Court application` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the order does not so require: the text says nothing

-- Under section 12C(1), may I, as an officer of the company, notify the Registrar of the error
#ASSERT `Under section 12C(1), may I, as an officer of the company, notify the Registrar of the error` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(a) any error contained in any document relating to the company filed or lodged with the Registrar"
