#ASSERT `Under section 12D(6), may the Registrar remove the notation` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not satisfied: a failed "if" gating a grant

-- Under section 12D(7), may the Registrar by written notice request the company or its officers to take steps within a time the Registrar specifies
#ASSERT `Under section 12D(7), may the Registrar by written notice request the company or its officers to take steps within a time the Registrar specifies` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "Despite anything in this section, the Registrar may, if the Registrar is satisfied that there is any error, defect or inaccuracy ..., by written notice, request"
#ASSERT `Under section 12D(7), may the Registrar by written notice request the company or its officers to take steps within a time the Registrar specifies` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not satisfied: a failed "if" gating a grant

§ `My residential address kept from public access (sections 12E and 12F)`

-- Under section 12E(1), must the Registrar cause my residential address to be excluded from public access
#ASSERT `Under section 12E(1), must the Registrar cause my residential address to be excluded from public access` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "the residential address of a director, chief executive officer or secretary of a company contained in the register of directors, register of chief executive officers or register of secretaries"
#ASSERT `Under section 12E(1), must the Registrar cause my residential address to be excluded from public access` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "the residential address of a member of a private company, who is an individual, contained in the electronic register of members"
#ASSERT `Under section 12E(1), must the Registrar cause my residential address to be excluded from public access` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an address of another kind: the text says nothing (limited by its own wording)

-- Under section 12E(2), may the Registrar cause my residential address to cease to be excluded from public access
#ASSERT `Under section 12E(2), may the Registrar cause my residential address to cease to be excluded from public access` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "Where, pursuant to subsection (1) or (3), the residential address ... is excluded from public access ..., the Registrar may cause the residential address to cease to be excluded ... in accordance with section 12F"
#ASSERT `Under section 12E(2), may the Registrar cause my residential address to cease to be excluded from public access` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- excluded, but the Registrar has not followed section 12F: the text says nothing of an exercise "in accordance with section 12F" that is not (grant ruling, limit 1)
#ASSERT `Under section 12E(2), may the Registrar cause my residential address to cease to be excluded from public access` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the address is not so excluded: a failed "Where" (periods ruling (b); split site (ii))
#ASSERT `Under section 12E(2), may the Registrar cause my residential address to cease to be excluded from public access` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not so excluded and section 12F not followed: the failed "Where" decides first

