#ASSERT `Under section 12F(6), must the notice to me be sent to my residential address` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "unless it appears to the Registrar that service at that address may be ineffective to bring it to the individual's notice"

-- Under section 12F(6), may the notice be sent to another last known address of mine
#ASSERT `Under section 12F(6), may the notice be sent to another last known address of mine` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "in which case it may be sent to any other last known address of that individual"
#ASSERT `Under section 12F(6), may the notice be sent to another last known address of mine` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- service at the residential address does not appear ineffective: the text says nothing of another address (the first limb governs)

-- Under section 12F(7), may I appeal to the Court against the decision
#ASSERT `Under section 12F(7), may I appeal to the Court against the decision` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "within 30 days after the date of receiving the notice": 1 March plus 30 days is 31 March, the last day in time
#ASSERT `Under section 12F(7), may I appeal to the Court against the decision` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the day of receipt is in time (fork line F-H-P2)
#ASSERT `Under section 12F(7), may I appeal to the Court against the decision` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- one day late: a period the text fixes in its own words (periods ruling (a))
#ASSERT `Under section 12F(7), may I appeal to the Court against the decision` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 28 2 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- before the notice was received: no appeal yet lies
#ASSERT `Under section 12F(7), may I appeal to the Court against the decision` FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING   -- not aggrieved: the right is "Any individual aggrieved by the decision" (limited by its own wording)

-- Under section 12F(7), may the Court confirm or reverse the decision of the Registrar and make any directions in the matter
#ASSERT `Under section 12F(7), may the Court confirm or reverse the decision of the Registrar and make any directions in the matter` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "the Court may confirm or reverse the decision of the Registrar and make such directions in the matter as it thinks fit"
#ASSERT `Under section 12F(7), may the Court confirm or reverse the decision of the Registrar and make any directions in the matter` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no appeal brought within the period: the text says nothing of the Court's power outside an appeal

-- Under section 12F(8), am I barred from providing a contact address
#ASSERT `Under section 12F(8), am I barred from providing a contact address` (Date 10 1 2026) (Date 10 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "within 3 years after": the day of the cessation is inside the period (fork line F-H-P2)
#ASSERT `Under section 12F(8), am I barred from providing a contact address` (Date 10 1 2026) (Date 10 1 2029) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the last day of the 3 years: 10 January 2026 plus 3 years is 10 January 2029
#ASSERT `Under section 12F(8), am I barred from providing a contact address` (Date 10 1 2026) (Date 11 1 2029) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- one day after the 3 years: a period the text fixes in its own words (periods ruling (a))
#ASSERT `Under section 12F(8), am I barred from providing a contact address` (Date 10 1 2026) (Date 9 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- before the cessation: the 3 years have not begun
#ASSERT `Under section 12F(8), am I barred from providing a contact address` (Date 10 1 2026) (Date 10 6 2027) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "unless the Registrar is satisfied that there is good cause": inside the 3 years, good cause shown
#ASSERT `Under section 12F(8), am I barred from providing a contact address` (Date 10 1 2026) (Date 10 6 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- inside the 3 years, no good cause: barred

-- Under section 12F(9), must the Registrar replace my contact address in each register kept under section 12(1) with the new contact address
#ASSERT `Under section 12F(9), must the Registrar replace my contact address in each register kept under section 12(1) with the new contact address` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "Where an individual provides a new contact address under any ACRA administered Act, the Registrar must replace the individual's contact address in each register kept under section 12(1)"
#ASSERT `Under section 12F(9), must the Registrar replace my contact address in each register kept under section 12(1) with the new contact address` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "Subject to subsection (8)": barred, so no replacement is owed
#ASSERT `Under section 12F(9), must the Registrar replace my contact address in each register kept under section 12(1) with the new contact address` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no new contact address provided: a failed "where"

§ `Making good a default, relodging lost documents, the form of documents (sections 13 to 15)`

-- Under section 13(1), did the corporation or person fail to make good the default within 14 days after the service of the notice
#ASSERT `Under section 13(1), did the corporation or person fail to make good the default within 14 days after the service of the notice` (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) EQUALS TRUE   -- never made good
#ASSERT `Under section 13(1), did the corporation or person fail to make good the default within 14 days after the service of the notice` (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS FALSE   -- made good on the 14th day after service (1 March plus 14 days is 15 March): within 14 days after
#ASSERT `Under section 13(1), did the corporation or person fail to make good the default within 14 days after the service of the notice` (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 16 3 2026) EQUALS TRUE   -- made good one day later: not within 14 days after
#ASSERT `Under section 13(1), did the corporation or person fail to make good the default within 14 days after the service of the notice` (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS FALSE   -- made good on the day of service: in time (fork line F-H-P2)

-- Under section 13(1), may the Court order the corporation and any officer of the corporation or such person to make good the default
#ASSERT `Under section 13(1), may the Court order the corporation and any officer of the corporation or such person to make good the default` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(a) any provision of this Act or of any other law ... which requires the filing or lodging ... of any return, account or other document", failing to make good within 14 days, on application by a member or creditor or by the Registrar
#ASSERT `Under section 13(1), may the Court order the corporation and any officer of the corporation or such person to make good the default` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(b) any request of the Registrar to amend or complete and resubmit any document or to submit a fresh document"
#ASSERT `Under section 13(1), may the Court order the corporation and any officer of the corporation or such person to make good the default` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(c) any request of the Registrar under section 12D(7)"
#ASSERT `Under section 13(1), may the Court order the corporation and any officer of the corporation or such person to make good the default` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "(other than the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018)": paragraph (a) is closed in the text's own words
#ASSERT `Under section 13(1), may the Court order the corporation and any officer of the corporation or such person to make good the default` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- under the IRDA for (a), but a default under (b) stands alone
#ASSERT `Under section 13(1), may the Court order the corporation and any officer of the corporation or such person to make good the default` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- made good in time: a failed "If" gating a grant (grant ruling, limit 1)
#ASSERT `Under section 13(1), may the Court order the corporation and any officer of the corporation or such person to make good the default` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the applicant is none of the three: limited by its own wording
#ASSERT `Under section 13(1), may the Court order the corporation and any officer of the corporation or such person to make good the default` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a default of no kind the subsection names: the text says nothing

-- Under section 13(2), may the order provide that all costs of and incidental to the application must be borne by the person I name
#ASSERT `Under section 13(2), may the order provide that all costs of and incidental to the application must be borne by the person I name` TRUE `s 13(2) the corporation` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "must be borne by the corporation"
#ASSERT `Under section 13(2), may the order provide that all costs of and incidental to the application must be borne by the person I name` TRUE `s 13(2) such person` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "or by such person"
#ASSERT `Under section 13(2), may the order provide that all costs of and incidental to the application must be borne by the person I name` TRUE `s 13(2) an officer of the corporation` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "by any officer of the corporation responsible for the default"
#ASSERT `Under section 13(2), may the order provide that all costs of and incidental to the application must be borne by the person I name` TRUE `s 13(2) an officer of the corporation` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an officer not responsible: limited by its own wording
#ASSERT `Under section 13(2), may the order provide that all costs of and incidental to the application must be borne by the person I name` TRUE `s 13(2) someone else` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another bearer: the list does not say "only" (list not closed)
#ASSERT `Under section 13(2), may the order provide that all costs of and incidental to the application must be borne by the person I name` FALSE `s 13(2) the corporation` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not an order under subsection (1): "Any such order"

-- Under section 13(3), does section 13 limit the operation of the written law
#ASSERT `Under section 13(3), does section 13 limit the operation of the written law` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "Nothing in this section limits the operation of any written law imposing penalties"
#ASSERT `Under section 13(3), does section 13 limit the operation of the written law` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another law: the text says nothing

-- Under section 14(1), may the corporation apply to the Registrar for permission to lodge a copy of the document as originally filed or lodged
#ASSERT `Under section 14(1), may the corporation apply to the Registrar for permission to lodge a copy of the document as originally filed or lodged` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "the constitution or any other document relating to the corporation filed or lodged with the Registrar has been lost or destroyed"
#ASSERT `Under section 14(1), may the corporation apply to the Registrar for permission to lodge a copy of the document as originally filed or lodged` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- nothing lost or destroyed: a failed "If" gating a grant (grant ruling, limit 1)
#ASSERT `Under section 14(1), may the corporation apply to the Registrar for permission to lodge a copy of the document as originally filed or lodged` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not incorporated or registered under this Act or a corresponding previous law: the text says nothing

-- Under section 14(2), may the Registrar direct notice of the application to be given to such persons and in such manner as the Registrar thinks fit
#ASSERT `Under section 14(2), may the Registrar direct notice of the application to be given to such persons and in such manner as the Registrar thinks fit` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "On such application being made the Registrar may direct notice thereof to be given"
#ASSERT `Under section 14(2), may the Registrar direct notice of the application to be given to such persons and in such manner as the Registrar thinks fit` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no application made: a failed "when" (periods ruling (b); split site (ii))

-- Under section 14(3), may the Registrar certify upon the copy that the Registrar is so satisfied and direct that the copy be lodged in the manner required by law in respect of the original
#ASSERT `Under section 14(3), may the Registrar certify upon the copy that the Registrar is so satisfied and direct that the copy be lodged in the manner required by law in respect of the original` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(a) ...; (b) ...; and (c) ..." all met
#ASSERT `Under section 14(3), may the Registrar certify upon the copy that the Registrar is so satisfied and direct that the copy be lodged in the manner required by law in respect of the original` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (a) unmet: a failed "upon being satisfied" (periods ruling (b); split site (ii))
#ASSERT `Under section 14(3), may the Registrar certify upon the copy that the Registrar is so satisfied and direct that the copy be lodged in the manner required by law in respect of the original` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (b) unmet
#ASSERT `Under section 14(3), may the Registrar certify upon the copy that the Registrar is so satisfied and direct that the copy be lodged in the manner required by law in respect of the original` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (c) unmet

-- Under section 14(4), does the copy for all purposes have the same force and effect as the original
#ASSERT `Under section 14(4), does the copy for all purposes have the same force and effect as the original` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "Upon the lodgment, that copy for all purposes has ... the same force and effect as the original"
#ASSERT `Under section 14(4), does the copy for all purposes have the same force and effect as the original` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not lodged: a failed "upon" (periods ruling (b))

