#ASSERT `Under section 14(5), may the order of the Court be lodged with the Registrar` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "the order may be lodged with the Registrar"
#ASSERT `Under section 14(5), may the order of the Court be lodged with the Registrar` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not an order under this subsection: the text says nothing

-- Under section 14(5), must the Registrar register the order
#ASSERT `Under section 14(5), must the Registrar register the order` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "must be registered by the Registrar"
#ASSERT `Under section 14(5), must the Registrar register the order` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not lodged: the duty does not arise (marginal reading (a))

-- Under section 14(5), is the payment, contract, dealing, act or thing invalidated or affected by the variation or rescission
#ASSERT `Under section 14(5), is the payment, contract, dealing, act or thing invalidated or affected by the variation or rescission` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "no payments, contracts, dealings, acts and things made, had or done in good faith before the registration of such order and upon the faith of and in reliance upon the certificate are invalidated or affected"
#ASSERT `Under section 14(5), is the payment, contract, dealing, act or thing invalidated or affected by the variation or rescission` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not in good faith: the saving does not speak
#ASSERT `Under section 14(5), is the payment, contract, dealing, act or thing invalidated or affected by the variation or rescission` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- after the registration of the order: the saving does not speak
#ASSERT `Under section 14(5), is the payment, contract, dealing, act or thing invalidated or affected by the variation or rescission` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not in reliance upon the certificate: the saving does not speak
#ASSERT `Under section 14(5), is the payment, contract, dealing, act or thing invalidated or affected by the variation or rescission` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no variation or rescission: the sentence does not speak

-- Under section 14(6), is a fee payable upon the lodging of the document
#ASSERT `Under section 14(6), is a fee payable upon the lodging of the document` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "No fee is payable upon the lodging of a document under this section"
#ASSERT `Under section 14(6), is a fee payable upon the lodging of the document` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a document lodged otherwise: the text says nothing

-- Under section 15(2), may the Registrar serve on the person a notice stating the Registrar's opinion and the requirements with which the document does not comply
#ASSERT `Under section 15(2), may the Registrar serve on the person a notice stating the Registrar's opinion and the requirements with which the document does not comply` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "the Registrar may serve on any person by whom under that provision the document was required to be delivered ... a notice"
#ASSERT `Under section 15(2), may the Registrar serve on the person a notice stating the Registrar's opinion and the requirements with which the document does not comply` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a person who was not required to deliver it: the text says nothing
#ASSERT `Under section 15(2), may the Registrar serve on the person a notice stating the Registrar's opinion and the requirements with which the document does not comply` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the Registrar holds no such opinion: a failed "If" gating a grant (grant ruling, limit 1)
#ASSERT `Under section 15(2), may the Registrar serve on the person a notice stating the Registrar's opinion and the requirements with which the document does not comply` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no document delivered under the Act: the text says nothing

-- Under section 15(3)(a), is the duty to deliver the document treated as not having been discharged by the delivery of that document
#ASSERT `Under section 15(3)(a), is the duty to deliver the document treated as not having been discharged by the delivery of that document` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "any duty imposed by that provision to deliver such a document to the Registrar is to be treated as not having been discharged by the delivery of that document"
#ASSERT `Under section 15(3)(a), is the duty to deliver the document treated as not having been discharged by the delivery of that document` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no notice served under subsection (2): a failed "Where" (periods ruling (b); split site (ii)); the answer means only that this deeming does not apply

-- Under section 15(4), what is the last day of the period mentioned in subsection (3)(b)
#ASSERT `Under section 15(4), what is the last day of the period mentioned in subsection (3)(b)` (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) EQUALS Date 24 2 2026   -- "ending on the 14th day after the date of service of the notice": 10 February plus 14 days is 24 February
#ASSERT `Under section 15(4), what is the last day of the period mentioned in subsection (3)(b)` (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 20 2 2026) EQUALS Date 6 3 2026   -- 20 February plus 14 days is 6 March (28 days in February 2026)

-- Under section 15(4), does the day fall within the period mentioned in subsection (3)(b)
#ASSERT `Under section 15(4), does the day fall within the period mentioned in subsection (3)(b)` (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) EQUALS TRUE   -- "beginning on the day on which the document was delivered": the first day is in the period
#ASSERT `Under section 15(4), does the day fall within the period mentioned in subsection (3)(b)` (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 24 2 2026) EQUALS TRUE   -- the 14th day after service is the last day in the period
#ASSERT `Under section 15(4), does the day fall within the period mentioned in subsection (3)(b)` (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 25 2 2026) EQUALS FALSE   -- the day after the 14th day: outside
#ASSERT `Under section 15(4), does the day fall within the period mentioned in subsection (3)(b)` (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 31 1 2026) EQUALS FALSE   -- the day before the document was delivered: outside

