-- cases-seat questions from part sgi (wave 2; merged by the lead; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Cases for sgi-seat.l4: what a person in the seat would state, and the answer the text gives.
-- For each question: a yes case (JUST TRUE), the text's no case where the question has one (JUST FALSE), and a not-covered case where the question has one (NOTHING).
-- Every case is a layer-1 test case (sgi-tests-*.l4, with the expected value written from the text beside it) put to the seat question that calls that rule on the same plain inputs, so a seat question and its rule cannot disagree.
-- Dates are Date day month year; a "date asked" is the day the person is asking about.



