§§ `Sections 134 to 136: the register, the certificate, endorsement, satisfaction and release`

-- Under section 134(1): which particulars of the charge will be entered in the register.
#ASSERT count (`Under section 134(1), which particulars of the charge will be entered in the register` `s 134(1)(a) a charge to the benefit of which the holders of a series of debentures are entitled`) EQUALS 4      -- four particulars for a series of debentures
#ASSERT count (`Under section 134(1), which particulars of the charge will be entered in the register` `s 134(1)(b) any other charge existing on property acquired by the company`) EQUALS 4      -- four particulars for any other charge

-- Under section 134(3): must the Registrar issue to the company a certificate confirming the registration of the charge.
#ASSERT `Under section 134(3), must the Registrar issue to the company a certificate confirming the registration of the charge` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- application and fee
#ASSERT `Under section 134(3), must the Registrar issue to the company a certificate confirming the registration of the charge` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- no fee
#ASSERT `Under section 134(3), must the Registrar issue to the company a certificate confirming the registration of the charge` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- no application

-- Under section 135(1): must the company cause a copy of the notice of registration, or a statement of the registration and its date, to be endorsed on the debenture or certificate.
#ASSERT `Under section 135(1), must the company cause a copy of the notice of registration, or a statement of the registration and its date, to be endorsed on the debenture or certificate` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- issued after registration
#ASSERT `Under section 135(1), must the company cause a copy of the notice of registration, or a statement of the registration and its date, to be endorsed on the debenture or certificate` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- issued before the charge was registered
#ASSERT `Under section 135(1), must the company cause a copy of the notice of registration, or a statement of the registration and its date, to be endorsed on the debenture or certificate` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING      -- not a series debenture or certificate

-- Under section 135(3): am I guilty of the offence of authorising or permitting the delivery of an unendorsed debenture or certificate.
#ASSERT `Under section 135(3), am I guilty of the offence of authorising or permitting the delivery of an unendorsed debenture or certificate` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 135(3), am I guilty of the offence of authorising or permitting the delivery of an unendorsed debenture or certificate` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- not knowingly and wilfully (split site (i))
#ASSERT `Under section 135(3), am I guilty of the offence of authorising or permitting the delivery of an unendorsed debenture or certificate` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- endorsed as required

-- Under section 135(3): what is the most I can be fined for authorising or permitting the delivery of an unendorsed debenture or certificate, in Singapore dollars.
#ASSERT `Under section 135(3), what is the most I can be fined for authorising or permitting the delivery of an unendorsed debenture or certificate, in Singapore dollars` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST 2000      -- "a fine not exceeding $2,000"
#ASSERT `Under section 135(3), what is the most I can be fined for authorising or permitting the delivery of an unendorsed debenture or certificate, in Singapore dollars` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 136(1): may the company lodge with the Registrar a statement of satisfaction or release.
#ASSERT `Under section 136(1), may the company lodge with the Registrar a statement of satisfaction or release` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- (a)
#ASSERT `Under section 136(1), may the company lodge with the Registrar a statement of satisfaction or release` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- (b)
#ASSERT `Under section 136(1), may the company lodge with the Registrar a statement of satisfaction or release` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- "Where" neither (fork F-K7)

§§ `Section 137: extension of time and rectification`

-- Under section 137: may I apply to the Court for the extension of time or the rectification.
#ASSERT `Under section 137, may I apply to the Court for the extension of time or the rectification` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- the company
#ASSERT `Under section 137, may I apply to the Court for the extension of time or the rectification` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- a person interested
#ASSERT `Under section 137, may I apply to the Court for the extension of time or the rectification` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING      -- neither
