§ `Part 12 Division 2: offences (ss 401 to 406)`

-- Under section 401(1), is the corporation guilty of an offence for a misleading statement of its capital
-- a misleading statement is enough.
#ASSERT `Under section 401(1), is the corporation guilty of an offence for a misleading statement of its capital` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the capital is stated and the paid-up amount is as prominent: neither limb.
#ASSERT `Under section 401(1), is the corporation guilty of an offence for a misleading statement of its capital` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 401(1), is an officer of the corporation guilty of an offence for authorising a misleading statement of its capital
-- the facts of the layer-1 test in sgo-tests-offences.l4
#ASSERT `Under section 401(1), is an officer of the corporation guilty of an offence for authorising a misleading statement of its capital` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not knowingly: the officer is not caught.
#ASSERT `Under section 401(1), is an officer of the corporation guilty of an offence for authorising a misleading statement of its capital` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 401(1), what is the highest penalty on conviction for a misleading statement of capital
-- the facts of the layer-1 test in sgo-tests-offences.l4
#ASSERT `Under section 401(1), what is the highest penalty on conviction for a misleading statement of capital` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The subsection states no penalty: s 407(2) gives a fine of at most $1,000 and no imprisonment.
#ASSERT `Under section 401(1), what is the highest penalty on conviction for a misleading statement of capital` TRUE EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF 1000, 0, FALSE, FALSE)

-- Under section 401(3), am I deemed to have authorised the making of the statement because I voted for it at a meeting
-- (3): a vote in favour of the making of the statement is deemed to authorise it.
