-- Under section 409(3), may the proceedings for the offence be prosecuted in a District Court
-- the facts of the layer-1 test in sgo-tests-penalties.l4
#ASSERT `Under section 409(3), may the proceedings for the offence be prosecuted in a District Court` 6 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- District Court: "a term of 6 months or more".
#ASSERT `Under section 409(3), may the proceedings for the offence be prosecuted in a District Court` 5 EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 409(7), may a District Court impose a punishment authorised by the Act although it is greater than the Court is otherwise empowered to impose
-- the facts of the layer-1 test in sgo-tests-penalties.l4
#ASSERT `Under section 409(7), may a District Court impose a punishment authorised by the Act although it is greater than the Court is otherwise empowered to impose` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the facts of the layer-1 test in sgo-tests-penalties.l4
#ASSERT `Under section 409(7), may a District Court impose a punishment authorised by the Act although it is greater than the Court is otherwise empowered to impose` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 409A(1), may the Court grant an injunction restraining a person from engaging in conduct that contravenes the Act
-- the facts of the layer-1 test in sgo-tests-court.l4
#ASSERT `Under section 409A(1), may the Court grant an injunction restraining a person from engaging in conduct that contravenes the Act` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no conduct contravening the Act: the "Where" gate.
#ASSERT `Under section 409A(1), may the Court grant an injunction restraining a person from engaging in conduct that contravenes the Act` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- an application by a person whose interests are not affected.
#ASSERT `Under section 409A(1), may the Court grant an injunction restraining a person from engaging in conduct that contravenes the Act` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 409A(2), may the Court grant an injunction requiring a person to do an act or thing the Act requires
-- the facts of the layer-1 test in sgo-tests-court.l4
#ASSERT `Under section 409A(2), may the Court grant an injunction requiring a person to do an act or thing the Act requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the facts of the layer-1 test in sgo-tests-court.l4
#ASSERT `Under section 409A(2), may the Court grant an injunction requiring a person to do an act or thing the Act requires` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the facts of the layer-1 test in sgo-tests-court.l4
#ASSERT `Under section 409A(2), may the Court grant an injunction requiring a person to do an act or thing the Act requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 409A(3), may the Court grant an interim injunction pending the determination of the application
-- the facts of the layer-1 test in sgo-tests-court.l4
#ASSERT `Under section 409A(3), may the Court grant an interim injunction pending the determination of the application` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the facts of the layer-1 test in sgo-tests-court.l4
#ASSERT `Under section 409A(3), may the Court grant an interim injunction pending the determination of the application` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the facts of the layer-1 test in sgo-tests-court.l4
#ASSERT `Under section 409A(3), may the Court grant an interim injunction pending the determination of the application` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 409A(7), is the Court barred from requiring the undertaking as to damages
-- the facts of the layer-1 test in sgo-tests-court.l4
#ASSERT `Under section 409A(7), is the Court barred from requiring the undertaking as to damages` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the facts of the layer-1 test in sgo-tests-court.l4
#ASSERT `Under section 409A(7), is the Court barred from requiring the undertaking as to damages` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 409A(8), may the Court order a person to pay damages to any other person, in addition to or in substitution for the injunction
-- the facts of the layer-1 test in sgo-tests-court.l4
#ASSERT `Under section 409A(8), may the Court order a person to pay damages to any other person, in addition to or in substitution for the injunction` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the facts of the layer-1 test in sgo-tests-court.l4
#ASSERT `Under section 409A(8), may the Court order a person to pay damages to any other person, in addition to or in substitution for the injunction` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 409B(1), what is the highest sum the Registrar may collect to compound the offence
-- not prescribed as compoundable, or not reasonably suspected.
#ASSERT `Under section 409B(1), what is the highest sum the Registrar may collect to compound the offence` FALSE TRUE 50000 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1): the lower of half the maximum fine and $20,000.
#ASSERT `Under section 409B(1), what is the highest sum the Registrar may collect to compound the offence` TRUE TRUE 50000 EQUALS JUST 20000
-- half of $39,000 is $19,500: lower than $20,000.
#ASSERT `Under section 409B(1), what is the highest sum the Registrar may collect to compound the offence` TRUE TRUE 39000 EQUALS JUST 19500

-- Under section 409B(2), what is the highest sum the Registrar may collect to compound an offence that has ceased to be compoundable
-- the facts of the layer-1 test in sgo-tests-penalties.l4
#ASSERT `Under section 409B(2), what is the highest sum the Registrar may collect to compound an offence that has ceased to be compoundable` TRUE FALSE TRUE 30000 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): an offence that has ceased to be compoundable.
#ASSERT `Under section 409B(2), what is the highest sum the Registrar may collect to compound an offence that has ceased to be compoundable` TRUE TRUE TRUE 30000 EQUALS JUST 15000
-- the facts of the layer-1 test in sgo-tests-penalties.l4
#ASSERT `Under section 409B(2), what is the highest sum the Registrar may collect to compound an offence that has ceased to be compoundable` TRUE TRUE TRUE 100000 EQUALS JUST 20000

-- Under section 409B(3), may no further proceedings be taken against me in respect of the offence once I have paid the sum
-- (3): payment ends the proceedings.
#ASSERT `Under section 409B(3), may no further proceedings be taken against me in respect of the offence once I have paid the sum` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the facts of the layer-1 test in sgo-tests-penalties.l4
#ASSERT `Under section 409B(3), may no further proceedings be taken against me in respect of the offence once I have paid the sum` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 409C(1), may I appeal to the Court against the Registrar's act or decision
-- decision on 1 March 2025: 28 days after it ends on 29 March 2025.
#ASSERT `Under section 409C(1), may I appeal to the Court against the Registrar's act or decision` TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 29 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the facts of the layer-1 test in sgo-tests-court.l4
#ASSERT `Under section 409C(1), may I appeal to the Court against the Registrar's act or decision` TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 30 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not aggrieved.
#ASSERT `Under section 409C(1), may I appeal to the Court against the Registrar's act or decision` FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 5 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 409C(3), does section 409C not apply to the act or decision of the Registrar
-- the facts of the layer-1 test in sgo-tests-court.l4
#ASSERT `Under section 409C(3), does section 409C not apply to the act or decision of the Registrar` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the facts of the layer-1 test in sgo-tests-court.l4
#ASSERT `Under section 409C(3), does section 409C not apply to the act or decision of the Registrar` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
